{
  "_comment": [
    "FUNCTIONALLY LOAD-BEARING -- unlike reference/catalogue.json (display",
    "names only), this file DECIDES which Famly session gets booked. An empty",
    "or missing UUID here is not a cosmetic gap: it blocks the whole plan",
    "preview with a hard validation error naming exactly which path was",
    "missing, rather than booking the wrong session or none at all.",
    "",
    "Structure: institutions.<code>.funded.<variant>.<slot> and",
    "institutions.<code>.non_funded.<slot>. <code> is the `institution` field",
    "HubSpot sends (matched case-insensitively). <slot> is one of morning,",
    "afternoon, full_day (HubSpot may send 'full day' with a space -- the",
    "loader normalises it).",
    "",
    "<variant> describes what is MISSING from the funded session, not what is",
    "present:",
    "  with_meals_and_activities  has_meals=true,  has_activities=true",
    "  no_activities              has_meals=true,  has_activities=false",
    "  no_meals                   has_meals=false, has_activities=true",
    "  neither                    has_meals=false, has_activities=false",
    "",
    "The file is re-read on every call, so edits take effect without a server",
    "restart. Point SESSION_CATALOGUE_FILE elsewhere to override the path.",
    "Fill in each PASTE-... placeholder with the real Famly session UUID."
  ],
